description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, correct the field the trace execution identifier is read from, replacing a three line window.

The trace store endpoint has two success returns. Its success-sampled early return nests the identifier under a data object. Its normal return puts the identifier at the TOP level, shaped `{ success: true, execution_id, metrics }`. The capture reads only the nested form, so on every real response it is undefined, the guard beneath never fires, the variable it feeds stays null, and the report field fed from that variable is null on every compose. Nothing throws, because optional chaining yields undefined. Measured live: eleven rows created by this emission after deployment, every request answered 201 within 23 to 442 milliseconds, and the success line never logged once.

Replace these three consecutive lines, which may carry trailing whitespace:

      const traceBody = (await traceRes.json().catch(() => null)) as { data?: { execution_id?: string } } | null;
      const emittedId = traceBody?.data?.execution_id;
      if (typeof emittedId === "string" && emittedId.length > 0) {

with these three lines:

      const traceBody = (await traceRes.json().catch(() => null)) as { execution_id?: string; data?: { execution_id?: string } } | null;
      const emittedId = traceBody?.execution_id ?? traceBody?.data?.execution_id;
      if (typeof emittedId === "string" && emittedId.length > 0) {

Only the first two lines change. The third line is reproduced unchanged so that the replacement window includes the guard that consumes the binding. The widened type admits the top level field the endpoint actually returns; the widened read prefers it and keeps the nested form as a fallback so the sampled branch still works. The type annotation and the read must change together or the file will not typecheck. Everything below the guard, the enclosing catch, and the abort timeout are untouched.

One contiguous three line replacement, one file. Change nothing else.

